  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d01fd2d64a9249049aaa77d5c12a82fe, type: 3}
  m_Name: MCQ_004
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::MCQQuestionData
  questionText: 'The cupula in the semicircular canal will be bent when a rotation
    begins. This is because:'
  referenceImage: {fileID: 0}
  explanationText: When the semicircular canals in the inner ear experience angular
    acceleration, the endolymph fluid inside the canals initially lags behind the
    movement of the canal walls, causing the cupula (a sensory structure within the
    canal) to bend. This bending stimulates hair cells and signals changes in rotational
    movement.
  options:
  - The fluid (endolymph) within the semicircular canal lags behind the accelerated
    canal walls
  - The cupula will stay in place and give the correct impression
  - The fluid (endolymph) will precede the accelerated canal walls
  - The cupula will bend on constant angular speeds
  correctOptionIndex: 0
